    "intro_html":  "Chicken Divan started life at a fancy New York hotel and got adopted by every church potluck in America, which is usually a sign a dish is genuinely good. Chicken and broccoli under a cheddar and sour cream sauce, topped with buttered bread crumbs and baked until it bubbles at the edges. You mix it cold, put it in the oven, and walk away. Each serving lands at 566 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e34 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.06 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
